IMPORT prelude

-- Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (Singapore) -- electronic records, writing, signature, retention,
-- originals, contract formation, time of despatch and receipt, and input errors: ss 2 to 16 and the
-- First Schedule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ETA2010.txt (amendments up to Act 38 of 2022, and S 10/2025 in the Third
-- Schedule).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. 33 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository cite it. It is the Act that
-- decides whether an email, a click-through or a PDF signature counts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electronic Transactions Act 2010 -- records and contracts`

§§ `4 and the First Schedule -- what Part 2 does not reach`

-- s 4(1): "The provisions of this Act specified in the first column of the First Schedule do not apply to
-- any rule of law requiring writing or signatures in any of the matters specified in the second column".
-- First Schedule, every item in the first column is "Part 2":
--   1. "The creation or execution of a will"
--   2. "The creation, performance or enforcement of an indenture, declaration of trust or power of attorney,
--       with the exception of implied, constructive and resulting trusts and a lasting power of attorney defined
--       under section 2(1) of the Mental Capacity Act 2008"
--   3. "Any contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property, or any interest in such property"
--   4. "The conveyance of immovable property or the transfer of any interest in immovable property."
--
-- The exclusion bites only on a rule of law REQUIRING WRITING OR SIGNATURES. Where no such rule applies to the
-- matter, Part 2 is not needed and the Schedule does nothing.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `a will`
    `an express declaration of trust`
    `an implied, constructive or resulting trust`
    `an ordinary power of attorney`
    `a lasting power of attorney`
    `an indenture`
    `a contract for the sale of an interest in immovable property`
    `a conveyance of immovable property`
    `a tenancy agreement`
    `a contract for the sale of goods`
    `a guarantee`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter is excluded from Part 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a will` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an express declaration of trust` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ordinary power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an indenture` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contract for the sale of an interest in immovable property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a conveyance of immovable property` THEN TRUE
    -- "or other disposition of ... any interest in such property": a tenancy is a disposition of an interest in
    -- immovable property. The text gives no carve-out for short leases.
    WHEN `a tenancy agreement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5 -- party autonomy`

-- s 5(2): nothing in Part 2 prevents the parties "(a) excluding the use of electronic records, electronic
-- communications or electronic signatures in the contract or transaction by agreement; or (b) imposing additional
-- requirements as to the form or authentication".
-- s 5(3): the parties may by agreement "(a) exclude section 6, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15 or 16 from applying ...; or
-- (b) derogate from or vary the effect of all or any of those provisions".
--
-- s 5(3) names ss 6 and 11 to 16, and leaves out ss 7 to 10 (writing, signature, retention, originals). Those are
-- rules about satisfying a RULE OF LAW, and the parties cannot by contract vary what satisfies the law. They can
-- still refuse electronic dealing altogether under s 5(2)(a).
DECLARE Section IS ONE OF
    `section 6, legal recognition`
    `section 7, writing`
    `section 8, signature`
    `section 9, retention`
    `section 10, originals`
    `section 11, contract formation`
    `section 12, effectiveness between parties`
    `section 13, time and place of despatch and receipt`
    `section 14, invitation to make offer`
    `section 15, automated message systems`
    `section 16, input error`

GIVEN `the section` IS A Section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parties may contract out of the section under section 5(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 7, writing` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 8, signature` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 9, retention` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 10, originals` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 5(1): consent to the form of a communication "may be inferred from the conduct of the parties".
GIVEN `consent was expressly given` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent can be inferred from conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parties consented to the form` IF
    `consent was expressly given` OR `consent can be inferred from conduct`

§§ `7 and 8 -- writing and signature`

-- s 7: where a rule of law requires writing, "an electronic record satisfies that rule of law if the information
-- contained in the electronic record is ACCESSIBLE SO AS TO BE USABLE FOR SUBSEQUENT REFERENCE."
-- s 8: where a rule of law requires a signature, the requirement is satisfied in relation to an electronic record if
-- "(a) a method is used to IDENTIFY the person and to INDICATE that person's INTENTION in respect of the information
-- ...; and (b) the method used is either -- (i) AS RELIABLE AS APPROPRIATE for the purpose ..., in the light of all
-- the circumstances, including any relevant agreement; or (ii) PROVEN IN FACT to have fulfilled the functions
-- described in paragraph (a), by itself or together with further evidence."
--
-- The (ii) limb means an unreliable method is enough if it in fact identified the person and showed their intention:
-- a typed name at the foot of an email, proved by the surrounding correspondence.
DECLARE ElectronicDocument HAS
    `the matter` IS A Matter
    `accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a method identifies the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method indicates the person's intention as to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method is as reliable as appropriate for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method is proven in fact to have identified the person and shown intention` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the document` IS AN ElectronicDocument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the electronic record satisfies a writing requirement` IF
        NOT `the matter is excluded from Part 2` (`the document`'s `the matter`)
    AND `the document`'s `accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference`

GIVEN `the document` IS AN ElectronicDocument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the electronic signature satisfies a signature requirement` IF
        NOT `the matter is excluded from Part 2` (`the document`'s `the matter`)
    AND `the document`'s `a method identifies the person`
    AND `the document`'s `the method indicates the person's intention as to the information`
    AND (    `the document`'s `the method is as reliable as appropriate for the purpose`
         OR  `the document`'s `the method is proven in fact to have identified the person and shown intention`)

§§ `9 -- retention`

-- s 9(1): a retention requirement is satisfied by an electronic record if (a) the information remains accessible so as
-- to be usable for subsequent reference; (b) it is retained in the original format or one demonstrably accurate;
-- (c) information identifying origin, destination, date and time of sending or receipt is retained; and (d) any
-- additional requirements of the supervising public agency are complied with.
-- s 9(2): (c) "does not extend to any information necessarily and automatically generated solely for the purpose of
-- enabling a record to be sent or received" -- routing headers need not be kept.
-- s 9(3): a person may use another's services. s 9(4): the section does not apply to a rule that itself provides for
-- electronic retention, or one excluded by Ministerial order.
DECLARE Retention HAS
    `remains accessible for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept in the original format or one shown to be accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `origin, destination and time of sending or receipt are kept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supervising agency's additional requirements are met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rule itself provides for electronic retention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has excluded the rule by order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `retained through a third-party service` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the retention` IS A Retention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 applies to the retention requirement` IF
        NOT `the retention`'s `the rule itself provides for electronic retention`
    AND NOT `the retention`'s `the Minister has excluded the rule by order`

GIVEN `the retention` IS A Retention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `electronic retention satisfies the requirement under section 9` IF
        `section 9 applies to the retention requirement` `the retention`
    AND `the retention`'s `remains accessible for subsequent reference`
    AND `the retention`'s `kept in the original format or one shown to be accurate`
    AND `the retention`'s `origin, destination and time of sending or receipt are kept`
    AND `the retention`'s `the supervising agency's additional requirements are met`

§§ `10 -- originals`

-- s 10(1): an "original form" requirement is satisfied by an electronic record if (a) there is "a reliable assurance as
-- to the integrity of the information ... from the time [it] was first made in its final form"; (b) where it is to be
-- provided to a person, it is capable of being displayed to them; and (c) any supervising agency's additional
-- requirements are met. s 10(2)(a): integrity means "complete and unaltered, apart from the introduction of any changes
-- that arise in the normal course of communication, storage and display".
DECLARE Original HAS
    `there is a reliable assurance the information is complete and unaltered since final form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only changes arise in the normal course of communication, storage and display` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is to be provided to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it can be displayed to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supervising agency's additional requirements are met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has excluded the rule by order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the record` IS AN Original
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the electronic record satisfies an original-form requirement` IF
        NOT `the record`'s `the Minister has excluded the rule by order`
    AND `the record`'s `there is a reliable assurance the information is complete and unaltered since final form`
    AND `the record`'s `the only changes arise in the normal course of communication, storage and display`
    AND (    NOT `the record`'s `it is to be provided to a person`
         OR  `the record`'s `it can be displayed to that person`)
    AND `the record`'s `the supervising agency's additional requirements are met`

§§ `11, 12, 15 -- contracts`

-- s 11(2): a contract "is not to be denied validity or enforceability SOLELY on the ground that an electronic
-- communication was used". s 15: the same for contracts formed by automated message systems with no natural person
-- reviewing. These only remove one ground of objection. Every other ground survives.
GIVEN `formed electronically` IS A BOOLEAN, `another ground of invalidity exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract may be denied validity` IF
    `another ground of invalidity exists`

§§ `13 -- time of despatch and receipt`

-- s 13(1): despatch is "(a) the time when it leaves an information system under the control of the originator ...;
-- or (b) if [it] has not left an information system under the control of the originator ..., the time when [it] is
-- received."
-- s 13(2): receipt at a DESIGNATED address is when it "becomes capable of being retrieved by the addressee".
-- s 13(3): receipt at an UNDESIGNATED address is when it becomes capable of being retrieved there "AND the addressee
-- BECOMES AWARE that the electronic communication has been sent to that address."
-- s 13(4): it is "presumed to be capable of being retrieved by the addressee when it reaches the electronic address".
-- s 13(5): deemed despatched at the originator's place of business and received at the addressee's.
--
-- Times are numbers here (minutes on a common clock). NOTHING stands for "has not happened".
DECLARE Communication HAS
    `left the originator's system at` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `reached the addressee's electronic address at` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the address was designated by the addressee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the addressee became aware it had been sent there at` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN `a` IS A MAYBE NUMBER, `b` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the later of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `x` THEN
        CONSIDER `b`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `y` THEN
            IF `x` GREATER THAN `y` THEN JUST `x` ELSE JUST `y`

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the time of receipt` MEANS
    IF `the communication`'s `the address was designated by the addressee`
    THEN `the communication`'s `reached the addressee's electronic address at`
    ELSE `the later of` (`the communication`'s `reached the addressee's electronic address at`) (`the communication`'s `the addressee became aware it had been sent there at`)

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the time of despatch` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the communication`'s `left the originator's system at`
    WHEN JUST `t` THEN JUST `t`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the time of receipt` `the communication`

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the communication has been received` IF
    CONSIDER `the time of receipt` `the communication`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `t` THEN TRUE

§§ `2(2) to (4) -- place of business`

-- s 2(3)(c) and (d): a location is not a place of business merely because servers are there or the system can be
-- accessed there, and "the sole fact that a party makes use of a domain name, an electronic mail address ... connected to
-- a specific country does not create a presumption that its place of business is located in that country."
GIVEN `the only link to the country is a domain name, email address or server` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the country is presumed to be the place of business` IF
    FALSE

§§ `14 -- website offers`

-- s 14: a proposal "not addressed to one or more specific parties, but generally accessible to parties making use of
-- information systems, including a proposal that makes use of interactive applications for the placement of orders",
-- is "an invitation to make offers, unless it clearly indicates the intention of the party making the proposal to be
-- bound in case of acceptance."
--
-- So the shop's website is not the offer; the customer's order is, and the shop accepts or not. A pricing error on a
-- website does not bind the shop on the customer's click, unless the site clearly said it would be bound.
DECLARE Proposal HAS
    `addressed to one or more specific parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `generally accessible to users of information systems` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clearly indicates an intention to be bound on acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposal is only an invitation to make offers` IF
        NOT `the proposal`'s `addressed to one or more specific parties`
    AND `the proposal`'s `generally accessible to users of information systems`
    AND NOT `the proposal`'s `clearly indicates an intention to be bound on acceptance`

§§ `16 -- input errors`

-- s 16(1): where "a NATURAL PERSON makes an input error in an electronic communication exchanged with the AUTOMATED
-- MESSAGE SYSTEM of another party and the automated message system DOES NOT PROVIDE the person with an OPPORTUNITY TO
-- CORRECT the error", the person "has the right to withdraw the PORTION of the electronic communication in which the
-- input error was made."
-- s 16(2): only if the person "(a) notifies the other party of the error AS SOON AS POSSIBLE after having learned of
-- the error ...; and (b) has not used or received any material benefit or value from the goods or services".
--
-- Four things follow from the text. A business's own employee typing into a supplier's portal is a natural person
-- and is covered. An error made to a HUMAN on the other side is not covered. A system that offered a confirmation
-- screen defeats the right, whether or not the person read it. And the right is to withdraw the erroneous PORTION,
-- not to rescind the whole contract.
DECLARE InputError HAS
    `made by a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party used an automated message system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the system gave an opportunity to correct the error` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified the other party as soon as possible after learning of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used or received material benefit from goods or services received` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the error` IS AN InputError
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may withdraw the erroneous portion` IF
        `the error`'s `made by a natural person`
    AND `the error`'s `the other party used an automated message system`
    AND NOT `the error`'s `the system gave an opportunity to correct the error`
    AND `the error`'s `notified the other party as soon as possible after learning of it`
    AND NOT `the error`'s `used or received material benefit from goods or services received`

GIVEN `the error` IS AN InputError
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 16 lets the person rescind the whole contract` IF
    FALSE
